WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:06.569
Arnn: This commencement is here to remind us
why we're here. What do we commence?

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:10.170
The subject of commencement is the good life.
The first graduating classes from

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:14.790
Hillsdale College graduated into a world
of the most disastrous war that our

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:19.830
country has ever known, and the question
is, "What can see them through both these

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:24.779
good times and the bad times that are
both bound to come to everyone in this

00:00:24.779 --> 00:00:32.149
audience today?" And the answer is virtue
and faith and freedom and knowledge.

00:00:32.149 --> 00:00:38.820
Esolen: Wherever I go the world will be a fallen
one, not because of this or that

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:44.190
political system, though some are much
better than others. It will be a fallen

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:51.449
world because I am in it. Human nature
has not changed. Ideas are actually

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:57.390
rather rare these days. We're full of
ideology but not ideas. Do not give to a

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:02.250
mere idea the love that you owe to
reality and the reverence you owe to God.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.210
In our time at Hillsdale College, we
sought truth and as we graduate and bring

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:09.780
the fruits of our perseverance we live
in a world that has lost sight of truth

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:13.470
in a very fundamental way. We have in
fact come to truth through experience,

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:17.520
through the experience of this community
of truth seekers. The liberal arts

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.670
education has made us capable of
understanding something about how the

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.840
world works. The more you learn the more
you ought to understand that you have so

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.440
much more to learn. Our learning will and can
never come to an end.

